# PicoCTF Writeup - Custom Wordlist Password Cracking with CUPP

## Challenge Overview

The challenge provided:

### Hash

```text
968c2349040273dd57dc4be7e238c5ac200ceac5
```

### Victim Information

```text
First Name: Alice
Surname: Johnson
Nickname: AJ
Birthdate: 15-07-1990
Partner's Name: Bob
Child's Name: Charlie
```

### Python Script

The script attempted to crack the SHA1 hash using a custom wordlist:

```python
if hashlib.sha1(password.encode()).hexdigest() == target_hash:
    return password
```

---

## Initial Analysis

The hash length was:

```text
40 characters
```

This indicated:

```text
SHA1
```

I first attempted to crack the hash using RockYou.

```bash
john --format=Raw-SHA1 --wordlist=/usr/share/wordlists/rockyou.txt hash.txt
```

Result:

```text
0g
```

No password found.

This suggested the password was not present in common password databases and required a targeted attack.

---

## Custom Wordlist Generation with CUPP

The challenge hinted:

```python
WORDLIST_FILE = "passwords.txt" # wordlist that was generated using CUPP
```

Generate a custom wordlist:

```bash
cupp -i
```

Input:

```text
First Name: Alice
Surname: Johnson
Nickname: AJ
Birthdate: 15071990
Partner's Name: Bob
Child's Name: Charlie
```

Enable:

```text
Special characters: Yes
Random numbers: Yes
Leet mode: Yes
```

CUPP generated a custom password list.

---

## Cracking the Hash

Run:

```bash
python3 check_password.py
```

Output:

```text
